# Rust build artifacts
target/
**/target/

# The guest is an excluded, separate build with its own target dir
predicate-engine/methods/guest/target/

# Lockfiles: keep the workspace + shared-types locks (apps), drop the guest's
# (it's a separate build; its lock is regenerated). Comment the next line out
# if you prefer to commit every lockfile.
# predicate-engine/methods/guest/Cargo.lock

# Proof / journal / image-id artifacts (binary outputs from runs)
*.bin
proof_seal.bin
journal.bin
image_id.txt

# Env / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# macOS
.DS_Store
__MACOSX/

# Editor / IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# Misc
*.log
artifacts/


# Regenerable AND version-dependent: seal/journal/image-id go stale the moment
# the predicate or the nssa/spel version changes, so a committed proof can
# silently become wrong. Reproduce via the prove example + the x86 wrap
# (see docs/dev-core-notes/). To commit a reference proof deliberately later:
#   git add -f predicate-engine/artifacts/seal.bin
predicate-engine/artifacts/